/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 72 0 R
/T ([  L_2={a^i bj^ cj^\\mid i,j\\geq0}  ]  1. Check \(L_1\)  [  L_1={a^i b^i c^k}  ]  Here, the number of as must equal the number of bs, while any number of cs is allowed. A CFG for \(L_1\) is:  [  S_1\\rightarrow AB  ]  [  A\\rightarrow aAb\\mid\\epsilon  ]  [  B\\rightarrow cB\\mid\\epsilon  ]  Therefore, \(L_1\) is context-free.  2. Check \(L_2\)  [  L_2={a^i bj^ cj^}  ]  Here, any number of as is allowed, while the number of bs must equal the number of cs. A CFG for \(L_2\) is:  [  S_2\\rightarrow AB  ]  [  A\\rightarrow aA\\mid\\epsilon  ]  [  B\\rightarrow bBc\\mid\\epsilon  ]  Therefore, \(L_2\) is also context-free.  3. Apply closure property  Context-free languages are closed under union.  Since  [  L=L_1\\cup L_2  ]  and both \(L_1\) and \(L_2\) are context-free, their union is also context-free.  Conclusion)
/E ([  L_2={a^i bj^ cj^\\mid i,j\\geq0}  ]  1. Check \(L_1\)  [  L_1={a^i b^i c^k}  ]  Here, the number of as must equal the number of bs, while any number of cs is allowed. A CFG for \(L_1\) is:  [  S_1\\rightarrow AB  ]  [  A\\rightarrow aAb\\mid\\epsilon  ]  [  B\\rightarrow cB\\mid\\epsilon  ]  Therefore, \(L_1\) is context-free.  2. Check \(L_2\)  [  L_2={a^i bj^ cj^}  ]  Here, any number of as is allowed, while the number of bs must equal the number of cs. A CFG for \(L_2\) is:  [  S_2\\rightarrow AB  ]  [  A\\rightarrow aA\\mid\\epsilon  ]  [  B\\rightarrow bBc\\mid\\epsilon  ]  Therefore, \(L_2\) is also context-free.  3. Apply closure property  Context-free languages are closed under union.  Since  [  L=L_1\\cup L_2  ]  and both \(L_1\) and \(L_2\) are context-free, their union is also context-free.  Conclusion)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
